From: Redmi 9 mainline port <lancelot@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] iio: adc: mt6359-auxadc: Take the ADC resolution into account in the scale

The scale currently only carries the reference voltage and the input
resistor divider ratio, so in_voltageY_raw * in_voltageY_scale is off
by 2^realbits, i.e. 4096 or 32768 times too large.

The vendor driver computes the value as

  val * r_ratio[0] * VOLT_FULL / r_ratio[1] >> res

so the resolution has to be part of the scale. Fold it into the
fractional denominator, which also makes the returned scale always
fractional.

The IIO core does not use scan_type.realbits when converting raw
values with iio_convert_raw_to_processed(), so consumers had no way to
correct this on their own.
---
 drivers/iio/adc/mt6359-auxadc.c

--- a/drivers/iio/adc/mt6359-auxadc.c
+++ b/drivers/iio/adc/mt6359-auxadc.c
@@ -774,14 +774,17 @@
 	int ret;
 
 	if (mask == IIO_CHAN_INFO_SCALE) {
+		/*
+		 * The raw value is the full resolution conversion result, so
+		 * the scale has to account for the ADC resolution as well:
+		 *   value = raw * vref * r_num / (r_div * 2^realbits)
+		 * Without the 2^realbits divisor, raw * scale overshoots the
+		 * real value by three to four orders of magnitude.
+		 */
 		*val = desc->r_ratio.numerator * cinfo->vref_mV;
+		*val2 = desc->r_ratio.denominator << chan->scan_type.realbits;
 
-		if (desc->r_ratio.denominator > 1) {
-			*val2 = desc->r_ratio.denominator;
-			return IIO_VAL_FRACTIONAL;
-		}
-
-		return IIO_VAL_INT;
+		return IIO_VAL_FRACTIONAL;
 	}
 
 	scoped_guard(mutex, &adc_dev->lock) {
